among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $404 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["American Airlines Group, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $8.7B market cap on $54.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $680M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"News sentiment sharply negative (-0.44) across 12 recent articles \u2014 the narrative has turned","sev":"red","cat":"news"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $5.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-5669689.27},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"FAA\u2019s nationwide ground stop strands travelers, causes confusion at LAX: \u2018Complete pandemonium\u2019","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/faa-nationwide-ground-stop-strands-234203000.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794614632.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.778,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Aviation expert warns 'no real end in sight' as all flights grounded across the US","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/aviation-expert-warns-no-real-233700000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794613650.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.772,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Nationwide ground stop happened just as FAA rolled out new AI tool","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/nationwide-ground-stop-happened-just-225837000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794613371.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.009,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MS NOW\u2019s Eugene Daniels \u2013 Stranded in LAX \u2013 Reports Fellow Passengers \u2018Shocked\u2019 at Trump\u2019s Silence on FAA Ground Stoppage","s